Mercuria is one of the world’s leading independent energy and commodity groups. Our purpose is to connect markets and to advance the energy transition. We bring markets together to support the world’s energy needs of today by trading, structuring finance, and investing into strategic assets, whilst generating over $170 billion in turnover. We are committed to advancing the transition to a more sustainable, affordable and reliable energy system for tomorrow. We are well ahead of the pledge we made in 2021 that over half of our investment capital will go into sectors that are advancing the energy transition by 2025, to contribute to global efforts to combat climate change.
Business Analysts are part of a global technology team, running an Agile delivery model in unison with our business partners to deliver multi-asset-class commodity systems, with a focus on automation, optimization, innovation, and control.
The role
We are looking for a Senior Business Analyst to join our dynamic IT department owning analysis and agile coordination for a range of projects in the Trading Technology team. You will report into the Head of Trading Technology working on a multi-year program of work developing best of breed proprietary solutions for our Traders, Desk Analysts, Middle Office, and Schedulers.
You will capture and analyze requirements, work with the development team to build a prioritized backlog, analyze problems, design solutions, and ultimately deliver tangible business value through strong engagement with our global user base.
You should have a delivery focused background, with a proven ability to manage stakeholders up to C-level, a track record of delivery multi-year projects, and a desire to identify and develop strategic solutions.
Key responsibilities
Ownership of the portfolio of requests, including all Change and Transformation Programs for Trading Technology, as well as associated day-to-day operational activities;
Drive delivery, whilst ensuring quality of low maintenance, high value solutions;
Collaboration with technology development team to produce, size, prioritize, and deliver a backlog of work in an agile manner;
Ensure requirements are correctly interpreted and offer maximum business value;
Actively seek to identify and drive improvements and innovation across both the business & IT operating models;
Represent and promote Mercuria IT, both internally and externally;
Support firm wide initiatives & strategy where required.
Job Requirements
5+ years of experience within a commodity trading environment;
Strong understanding of commodities business concepts and workflows;
Understanding technology project management best practice, and agile delivery with a passion for innovation;
Strong interpersonal skills - able to build relationships across the firm;
Analytical and critical thinking with ability to problem solve complex issues;
Excellent communication and influencing ability.
